[#:seon.task{:name "an-attempts-cluster-facts-copy-onto-main-by-identity"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Phase P1 of hybrid-agent-world.md (after P0 and P1a, `seon.db/entities-born-on-two-branches-of-one-commit-have-different-ids`: one eid counter per store, so a branch-born entity keeps its eid on main). The copy-back is git's squash merge over data (`merge --squash`: a three-way from the merge base, one commit on main, no parent link to the branch), never a cherry-pick and never datahike merge!/:parents. The pure `seon.cluster.squash/squash-merge` [source-db base-db target-db projection selection] -> {:tx-data :conflicts}: the branch's datoms since its merge base for `seon.program/cluster-attributes` (d/since on the branch; base = the immutable fork-point commit read with `datahike.api/commit-as-db` from `seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id`; `seon.cluster.registry/fork!` creates its roster ref with `datahike.api/branch!`, and `seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch!` deletes both refs. At Datahike revision 61bca1edd6bcef079f5c47e4f5f75df30549934d, `datahike.gc/reachable-in-branch` seeds each roster head and marks its indexes regardless of remove-before; only parent traversal is time limited. No attribute history retention change), restricted by selection to given identities (root's by-hand `seon.cluster.squash/squash-merge!`), grouped by entity, replayed with eids unchanged (every eid was issued by this store; `seon.db/an-explicit-eid-outside-the-allocators-range-is-refused` guards the rest) except the collision remap: a new entity whose :db.unique/identity value (`seon.db/identity-attributes`, looked up on main's AVET) already exists on main takes main's eid in its own datoms and in every ref to it, because Datahike refuses an explicit eid carrying another entity's unique value (:transact/unique) instead of upserting it; classified per [e a] as `seon.program/three-way` classifies digests: unchanged -> nothing, only theirs -> assert or retract, only ours -> keep, both and different -> the entity schema's :seon.cluster/conflict rule: :theirs asserts, :ours keeps, :add is one :db.fn/call that sums (the occurrence count), :root keeps ours plus a conflict row {entity attribute base ours theirs}. It reuses the merge-request machinery instead of a second comparison: the base comes from `seon.cluster.source/merge-base` and `seon.cluster.source/branch-base-t` (made public), and `seon.program/changed-identities` and `seon.program/digest-map` take a projection argument (program attributes for merge requests, cluster attributes here) so both are one three-way with two projections. Proofs, a table on values with d/with targets: this test (main pulls the end, the refined intent and a child task by eid); a-value-changed-on-both-sides-resolves-by-the-declared-rule (table over :root, :theirs, :add; under :root the entity's other attribute still copies); program-and-runtime-facts-never-copy (a defn, an evaluation, a turn and a received message yield empty tx-data); a-copy-of-an-unchanged-branch-is-empty; a-retraction-on-the-branch-retracts-on-an-unchanged-main-only; a-branch-born-entity-keeps-its-eid-on-main (the child task's eid on main equals its eid on the branch, refs included; main's next allocation is unmoved); a-natural-identity-born-on-both-sides-maps-to-mains-eid (two branches each mint an occurrence with one signature: main holds one entity under its own eid, count summed by :add, every ref remapped); the-merge-base-is-the-merge-requests (the squash's base commit equals `seon.cluster.source/merge-base` for the same branch); the-merge-base-retains-the-count-needed-by-add (base occurrence count 1, source 2, unchanged target 1 yields 2); a-base-ref-keeps-the-fork-commit-only-until-retirement (cutoff after fork retains the commit while the work branch exists; retirement removes both refs and collection removes the commit); cost row: a ten-evaluation attempt under 10 ms / 5 MB through seon.profile/measure. Files: src/seon/cluster/squash.clj, test/seon/cluster/squash_test.clj, src/seon/cluster/source.clj (merge-base public), src/seon/program.cljc (projection argument)."
             :must-read #{seon.program/three-way seon.program/changed-identities seon.program/digest-map seon.program/program-attributes seon.program/cluster-attributes seon.cluster.source/merge-base seon.cluster.registry/fork! seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! seon.cluster.registry/base-commit-id datahike.api/commit-as-db datahike.gc/gc-storage! seon.db/identity-attributes seon.db/with seon.profile/measure}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-agent-world.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/eid-ranges-opus.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/eid-ranges-sol.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-repeated-push-adds-nothing"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Phase U1 of hybrid-push.md (after U0; Opus lane, the one path). `seon.cluster.squash/push-tx` [db attempt head] runs inside main's writer as [:db.fn/call …]: it reads :seon.task.attempt/pushed from the writer's db (else the attempt's recorded fork commit :seon.task.attempt/fork), opens it with `datahike.api/commit-as-db` as the base, runs `seon.cluster.squash/squash-merge` with theirs = the held head and ours = the writer's db, keeps only the coordinates whose entity the attempt OWNS (its task and descendants by self-or-under over :seon.task/children, :seon.task/created-by = its agent, its attempt row by :seon.task/agent and merge request by :seon.task/of-assignment, messages by :seon.message/from or /to = its agent, occurrences naming it in :seon.error.occurrence/attempts; one pull per changed entity on theirs) and returns one transaction: the owned facts, [:db/add attempt :seon.task.attempt/pushed head-commit], one :seon.squash/finding per :root conflict (:conflict) and per changed coordinate it does not own (:unowned). :add is theirs minus base computed on ours inside the function (`add-count` is deleted); :max keeps the later of ours and theirs; a collision is remapped to main's eid whether or not base holds the entity (today's when-not base condition goes). pushed = head yields [] and the caller skips the transaction. `copy!`, `conflict-task!`, `squash-merge!`, `selected-coordinates` and `add-count` are deleted; `push!` [context attempt] is root's by-hand entrance. Proofs, a table on values with seon.db/with targets: this test (collision 1 -> 1 on a second push; a plain :add conflict 6 stays 6; tx-data []); a-push-of-an-advanced-branch-adds-only-its-new-delta (base 1, source 2, main 2 -> 3); a-root-edit-after-capture-is-a-conflict-not-overwritten (seon.db/with on a main edited after the head was captured: root's value stays, one :conflict finding carries base, ours, theirs, both commits); a-pushed-collision-stays-remapped (an occurrence pushed twice holds main's eid both times); an-edit-to-an-unowned-task-is-a-finding-not-a-push (the agent refines another task's intent: main's value unchanged, one :unowned finding names attempt, entity and attribute, its own refinement still lands); last-at-takes-the-later-of-both-sides; cost row through `seon.profile/measure`: push-tx under 8 ms warm for a ten-evaluation branch with one refinement, scanned datoms recorded (`seon.db/entities-changed-after` scans each CHANGED attribute's history; `seon.db/changed-attributes` skips the rest). Files: src/seon/cluster/squash.clj, test/seon/cluster/squash_test.clj."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.squash/squash-merge seon.cluster.squash/copy! seon.cluster.squash/add-count seon.program/changed-identities seon.program/three-way seon.db/changed-attributes seon.db/entities-changed-after seon.db/transact-call}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-push.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/verify-astra.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/plan-push-sol.md"}}]
